TEXT 616 456 Left 2 !.param Vdiff=1
TEXT 616 504 Left 2 ;When Lo-Z DM-termination is not allowed : \nThis circuit allows for low CM-termination, with little impact on DM-termination.\nIt could be placed between the CAN-connector (on the right in this schematic) and a CM-choke\n(which would be on the left)\nIf DC decoupling is needed, it causes a series LC-resonance, which short-circuits DM.\nThis can be damped by splitting the termination resistor as well.\nVcm phase set to 90° so that there's equal phase difference to both differential mode signals.
